# Chapter 8 token requests. Start the app first (see README.md): set Training__Password, then
# dotnet run (https://localhost:42108, Development). Use the same password here.
# Send the requests in order. Each "Expect" line is the status you should see.

@host = https://localhost:42108
@password = Learner-Pass-2026!

###
# The API requires a Bearer token. Expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/books/available

###
# A wrong password. Expect 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "learner@example.test", "password": "not-the-password" }

###
# Sign in for tokens. Expect 200 with accessToken and refreshToken
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "learner@example.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# Call the API with the access token. Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/books/available
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
# Exchange the refresh token for a new pair. Expect 200
# @name refreshed
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

###
# The first refresh token is now consumed. Expect 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

###
# The new access token works. Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/books/available
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshed.response.body.$.accessToken}}
